  "id": "Compound::DB01162 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "Terazosin, a selective alpha-1 adrenergic receptor antagonist, is shown to bind to Adra1a, a subunit of the alpha-1 adrenergic receptor. This binding is linked to the participation of Adra1a in the broader adrenergic receptor activity, which is subsequently participated by Adra1b. The evidence suggests that Terazosin may influence Adra1b through a shared pathway involving adrenergic receptor activity, potentially modulating its function. The varying scores across the paths indicate a consistent but not absolute relationship, with the core mechanism of Terazosin binding to Adra1a and its subsequent involvement in adrenergic receptor activity being the central link. The integration of these paths highlights a potential role for Terazosin in regulating Adra1b through the adrenergic receptor system, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains partially inferred.",
